      "message": "Maybe instead of \"if the file is cold, those reads are I/O-bound.\" say something like \"This scan involves reading close to the entire file in a scattered fashion. Doing such a read tends to not perform well I/O wise as it generally cannot take advantage of operating system level file system readahead. Reading the file sequentially up front tends to take advantage of readahead to fully populate the file system caches which then can make scattered reads much faster.\"",
